{"items":[{"targetId":"n0000350","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A node’s level is its nesting depth in the term-like parent–child structure, so descending through an application argument increases level by one.","densityScore":0.82,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Makes the level calculation behind the delta vector explicit."}]},{"targetId":"n0000356","injections":[{"type":"interpretation","text":"A delta is an address relative to the replicator’s sharing context: it identifies a consumer’s structural level, not a requested copy count.","densityScore":0.84,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Separates routing information from replication multiplicity."}]},{"targetId":"n0000362","injections":[{"type":"context","text":"Canonicalization is needed because core reduction can preserve computational meaning while temporarily destroying the restricted shape required for inverse translation.","densityScore":0.78,"relation":"supports","reason":"Explains why proper nets require a cleanup phase before back-translation."}]},{"targetId":"n0000367","injections":[{"type":"mechanism","text":"A discarded argument can become unreachable when an abstraction has no live variable occurrence that consumes that argument.","densityScore":0.8,"relation":"supports","reason":"Connects erased arguments to the disconnected material collected by the sweep."}]},{"targetId":"n0000386","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Two replicators are paired when a future interaction can require both agents to remain distinct; an unpaired replicator has no such remaining counterpart.","densityScore":0.66,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Supplies the pairing concept used by the merge safety condition."}]},{"targetId":"n0000392","injections":[{"type":"warrant","text":"An auxiliary port ending at an eraser has no remaining consumer, so retaining it cannot affect any value that remains reachable.","densityScore":0.81,"relation":"supports","reason":"Justifies why decay may remove eraser-bound exits."}]},{"targetId":"n0000399","injections":[{"type":"warrant","text":"Local confluence says competing core interactions can be reconciled, but it does not prescribe when nonlocal cleanup rewrites should run.","densityScore":0.85,"relation":"supports","reason":"Explains why a global priority rule is added despite confluence of the core."}]},{"targetId":"n0000402","injections":[{"type":"uncertainty","text":"Whether an early reducible pair will reach the scheduled position unchanged depends on a proof about intervening rewrites; it is not guaranteed merely because the pair is currently disjoint.","densityScore":0.76,"relation":"supports","reason":"Qualifies the safe-parallelism exception with its required invariant."}]},{"targetId":"n0000411","injections":[{"type":"mechanism","text":"If an argument is ignored, reducing inside that argument before its erasure performs work whose result cannot influence the enclosing normal form.","densityScore":0.84,"relation":"supports","reason":"States the causal reason leftmost-outermost order avoids wasted evaluation."}]},{"targetId":"n0000414","injections":[{"type":"mechanism","text":"Sharing replaces separate syntactic substitutions with multiple graph consumers connected to one evolving computation.","densityScore":0.83,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Explains how replicators avoid duplicated necessary work."}]},{"targetId":"n0000428","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Church–Rosser confluence concerns multi-step reduction paths: whenever two paths diverge from one state, both can be extended to a common state.","densityScore":0.86,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Makes the contrast with the one-step diamond property precise."}]},{"targetId":"n0000431","injections":[{"type":"interpretation","text":"Treating λ-terms as a projection means distinct net sharing structures may correspond to the same term-level computation.","densityScore":0.78,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Clarifies the claimed extra representational freedom of nets."}]},{"targetId":"n0000448","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A term is normalizing when at least one reduction sequence reaches a normal form; this does not imply that every possible sequence terminates.","densityScore":0.89,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Defines the existential quantifier underlying the claim."}]},{"targetId":"n0000476","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"An agent’s arity is its number of auxiliary ports, so passing through that agent can create one corresponding branch for each auxiliary connection.","densityScore":0.78,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Defines the quantity governing copying during commutation."}]},{"targetId":"n0000484","injections":[{"type":"interpretation","text":"Positive and negative deltas record whether an occurrence lies deeper or shallower than its replicator’s own level.","densityScore":0.83,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Gives an immediate reading of the delta sign."}]},{"targetId":"n0000486","injections":[{"type":"context","text":"Properness is a reachability classification rather than a normal-form condition: a proper net may still contain active interactions.","densityScore":0.82,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Separates intermediate reachability from completion."}]},{"targetId":"split-000001","injections":[{"type":"mechanism","text":"An outermost-first strategy delays work inside an argument until the enclosing application establishes that the argument is needed.","densityScore":0.82,"relation":"supports","reason":"Provides the operational mechanism behind avoiding discarded work."}]},{"targetId":"split-000002","injections":[{"type":"mechanism","text":"Several consumers can refer to one shared net region, allowing its reduction result to be propagated instead of independently recomputed.","densityScore":0.86,"relation":"supports","reason":"Provides the operational mechanism behind compute-once sharing."}]}]}
